[[Watch the selected player. Keeps following them after they respawn. Switches to a backup camera by itself if the game blocks the normal one.]],['Always Use Backup Spectate Camera']=
[[Spectate with our own orbit camera (right mouse to look, scroll to zoom). Use it if spectating looks wrong in a game.]],['Teleport to Target']='Teleport next to the selected player.',['Sort Players (Name / Distance)']=
[[Order the player list by name or by how close they are to you.]],['Copy Profile Link']=[[Copy the selected player's Roblox profile URL to your clipboard.]],['Save Outfit to Wardrobe']=
[[Save the selected player's avatar in the Wardrobe tab, to try on or buy later.]],['Sit On Head']='Sit on top of the selected player and stay there.',['Fling Target (Burst)']='Push the selected player with a short burst of velocity.',[
'Jumpscare Duration']=[[How long Jumpscare keeps you in front of the target before you snap back.]],['Jumpscare Target']=[[Teleport in front of the target's face, then return to where you were.]],['Chat Spam']=
[[Send the message in the box every 0.5 s. Chat filters and rate limits apply.]],['Follow Player']=
[[Walk after the selected player and stay near them. Finds a way around walls. Pauses while you walk yourself (WASD); click another player to switch.]],['Follow Distance']='How close Follow Player gets before it stops.',[
'Invisible (Server-side)']=[[Others can't see you; you play as a see-through copy. Turn off to come back.]],['Fly  (WASD + Space/Shift)']=[[Fly where the camera looks. Space/E up, Shift/Q down. Survives respawns.]],['Fly Speed']=
'How fast Fly moves you, in studs per second.',['Walk Speed']=[[Your walking speed (16 is normal). Re-applied after you respawn.]],['Jump Power']=[[How high you jump (50 is normal). Re-applied after you respawn.]],['Noclip']=
'Walk through walls and objects.',['Ctrl+Click Teleport']=[[Hold Ctrl and left-click anywhere in the world to teleport there.]],['Godmode']=[[Sets your health to infinite on your side. Many games still kill you server-side.]],[
'Infinite Jump']='Jump again in mid-air every time you press Space.',['Anti-Fling']=[[Cancels sudden huge sideways speed so other exploiters can't fling you.]],['Anti-AFK']=[[Stops Roblox from kicking you for being idle for 20 minutes.]],[
'Change UserId to Creator']=[[Locally pretend to be the game's creator. Only affects scripts on your side.]],['Give Jerk Tool']='Adds an animation tool to your backpack.',['Speed Boost']=
[[While you drive forward or back, pushes the vehicle up to Top Speed. Works on any car, boat or kart you drive yourself.]],['Top Speed']=[[The speed Speed Boost pushes you to. Nitro goes 50% over it, backing up gets half of it.]],[
'Acceleration']=[[How quickly Speed Boost gains speed, in studs per second, every second.]],['Nitro']=
[[While it's on and you drive forward: three times the acceleration, up to 1.5x Top Speed. Right-click it, give it a key and set the mode to Hold for a boost button.]],['Cruise Control']=
[[Holds the speed you drive at when you switch it on, uphill and downhill, also in cars that brake by themselves when you let go. Pressing forward raises it. Braking switches it off, and so does running into something. Right-click to give it a key.]]
,['Auto Dodge']=[[Watches the road ahead and steers into the nearest gap when a car or a wall is in the way; brakes when there is no gap. It doesn't know lanes or traffic rules, so it can still crash.]],['Dodge Closeness']=
[[How close Auto Dodge and Autopilot cut past things. Low keeps a wide gap and reacts early, high squeezes through late.]],['Autopilot']=
[[Drives by itself and dodges on the way. With no destination it drives around: it keeps to the kind of road it is on, stays away from edges and water, and takes a turning now and then. Type a saved place below, or press Drive on a row in the Teleports tab while you sit in the driver's seat, and it drives there. Switch it off to take over.]]
,['Autopilot Destination']=[[The saved place Autopilot drives to. Type a part of its name and press Enter. Leave it empty and Autopilot just drives around.]],['Autopilot Speed']=
[[How fast Autopilot drives on a clear, straight road. It slows down for turns and before it arrives.]],['Flying Car  (E up, Q down)']=
[[The car hovers and flies: forward and back along its nose, A / D turn it, E goes up, Q down. Switch it off near the ground: it drops.]],['Flight Speed']='How fast the Flying Car flies.',['Drive on Water']=
[[Water is solid under the car (only for you), so it drives across lakes and the sea.]],['Wall Driving']=[[The car sticks to whatever is under its wheels: drive at a wall and it climbs it. With nothing under the wheels it falls as usual.]],
['Instant Brake']=[[Pressing the other way than you're rolling stops the vehicle almost at once.]],['Turn Assist']=[[Turns the vehicle faster while you steer, so it corners sharply.]],['Turn Speed']=
[[How fast Turn Assist turns the vehicle, in degrees per second.]],['Extra Grip']=[[Takes away sideways sliding. 0% is the game's own grip, at 100% the vehicle never slides.]],['Downforce']=
[[Presses the vehicle onto the road, so it doesn't take off over bumps and hills.]],['Air Control']=[[In the air, steering turns the vehicle and forward / back tips its nose down / up.]],['Anti-Flip']=
[[Rolls the vehicle back onto its wheels when it leans over more than 60 degrees.]],['Flip Vehicle']=[[Put the vehicle you sit in back on its wheels, right where it is.]],['Drift']=
[[The car slides instead of gripping: its nose turns into the corner while it keeps travelling sideways. Right-click it, give it a key and set the mode to Hold for a handbrake-style drift button. Extra Grip pauses while you drift.]],[
'Drift Slide']=[[How long the car keeps sliding sideways. Low is a short slip, 100% is like ice.]],['Drift Steering']=[[How fast steering swings the car around while you drift, in degrees per second.]],['Max Drift Angle']=
[[The widest angle between where the car points and where it travels. Smaller is easier to control, 90 lets it go fully sideways.]],['Drift Power']=
[[Extra push along the car's nose while you slide and hold forward, so a drift doesn't die out. Stops at Top Speed, 0 turns it off.]],['Vehicle Jump']=[[Press the jump key while you drive to make the vehicle jump.]],['Vehicle Jump Key']=
[[The key that makes the vehicle jump. Click, then press the new key. (Space would make you leave the seat.)]],['Vehicle Jump Height']='How high the vehicle jumps, in studs.',['Vehicle Air Jumps']=
'Jump again in mid-air, as often as you press the key.',['Vehicle Gravity']=[[How heavy the vehicle is. 100% is normal, lower floats, at 0% it doesn't fall at all.]],['Speedometer']=
[[Shows how fast you move, on foot or in a vehicle. Drag it where you want it.]],['Speed Unit']='Studs per second, km/h or mph (a stud counts as 0.28 m).',['Keep Emote While Moving']=
[[Keep the emote going when you walk (on by default). Off = Roblox's normal behaviour: moving stops it.]],['Emote Speed']='Play emotes slower or faster.',['Reload Emote List']='Download the emote list again.',['Empty All Emote Folders']=
[[Take every emote out of every folder. The folders themselves stay.]],['Player ESP']=[[Turn the player ESP on. Pick what it shows in the Box, Text, Health and Extras sections.]],['Hide Teammates']=
[[Skip players on your team. Does nothing in games without teams.]],['Team Colors']="Colour the ESP and chams by each player's team colour.",['Visible Check']=
